e your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nIn the diagram, the area of rectangle $PQRS$ is $24.$ If $TQ = TR,$ what is the area of quadrilateral $PTRS?$ [asy]\nsize(100);\ndraw((0,0)--(6,0)--(6,4)--(0,4)--cycle);\ndraw((0,4)--(6,2));\ndraw((5.8,1.1)--(6.2,1.1));\ndraw((5.8,.9)--(6.2,.9));\ndraw((5.8,3.1)--(6.2,3.1));\ndraw((5.8,2.9)--(6.2,2.9));\nlabel(\"$P$\",(0,4),NW);\nlabel(\"$S$\",(0,0),SW);\nlabel(\"$R$\",(6,0),SE);\nlabel(\"$T$\",(6,2),E);\nlabel(\"$Q$\",(6,4),NE);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"8527fd0e991c3fca61b3c59f007735a5f92d41c0e732f7ca6fdad647e2c78e40"},"seconds":25.95333218574524,"seed":475585357038124854,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we first need to analyze the given information and the diagram. The rectangle \\(PQRS\\) has an area of 24. Since \\(TQ = TR\\), point \\(T\\) is the midpoint of segment \\(QR\\), which means it divides \\(QR\\) into two equal parts.\n\nLet's denote the length of \\(PQ\\) as \\(l\\) and the length of \\(PS\\) as \\(w\\). Therefore, the area of rectangle \\(PQRS\\) is given by:\n\\[\nl \\times w = 24\n\\]\n\nSince \\(T\\) is the midpoint of \\(QR\\), we have \\(QT = TR = \\frac{w}{2}\\).\n\nNow, we need to find the area of quadrilateral \\(PTRS\\). Notice that quadrilateral \\(PTRS\\) can be seen as the rectangle \\(PQRS\\) minus triangle \\(PQT\\).\n\nFirst, we calculate the area of triangle \\(PQT\\). The base of this triangle is \\(QT = \\frac{w}{2}\\) and the height is \\(PQ = l\\). The area of triangle \\(PQT\\) is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of } \\triangle PQT = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{w}{2} \\times l = \\frac{lw}{4}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(lw = 24\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of } \\triangle PQT = \\frac{24}{4} = 6\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of quadrilateral \\(PTRS\\) is the area of rectangle \\(PQRS\\) minus the area of triangle \\(PQT\\):\n\\[\n\\text{Area of } PTRS = 24 - 6 = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of quadrilateral \\(PTRS\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{18}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
